WEBVTT

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:06.470
Are you Henry?

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.880
Yes.

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:12.520
A girl named Mary called on the payphone and said she's at her parents and you're invited

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:13.510
to dinner.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:59.060
you wanted me to come or not. Where have you been? You never come around anymore.

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.040
Dinner's almost ready.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:32.980
Come on in.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.190
Hello there.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:08.180
Hello.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.180
I'm very pleased to meet you.

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:14.440
Sit down.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:48.310
- It's Henry, isn't it? - Yes.

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:11.210
- Mary tells me you're a very nice fellow.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:14.920
What do you do?

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:19.070
- Uh-oh, I'm on vacation.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:22.540
- What did you do?

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:27.040
- Oh, I'm sorry.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.320
Well, I work at LaPelle's factory.

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:43.630
printer and henry's very clever at printing yes he sounds very clever

00:20:43.630 --> 00:21:00.000
stranger got chicken tonight strangest damn thing

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:13.030
they're man-made little damn things smaller than my fists they're new i'm bill hello i'm henry

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:20.490
henry's at lapel's factory printing's your business huh mum it's mine 30 years i've seen

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:25.420
this neighborhood change from pastures to the hell hole it is now i put every damn pipe in this

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:30.000
neighborhood yeah bill now people think pipes grow in their home well they sure as hell

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:39.250
Are you hungry?

00:23:58.030 --> 00:24:00.000
have heard this before, but

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:04.950
Fourteen years ago, I had an operation on my arm here.

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:07.910
Doctors said I wouldn't be able to use it.

00:24:07.910 --> 00:24:10.170
"What the hell do they know?" I said.

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:13.220
And I rubbed it for a half hour every day.

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:16.700
And then I got so I could move it a little.

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:19.400
And I got so I could turn a faucet.

00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:22.940
And pretty soon I had my arm back again.

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:26.080
Now I can't feel a damn thing in it.

00:24:26.080 --> 00:24:27.270
All numb.

00:24:32.300 --> 00:24:34.680
I'm afraid to cut it, you know?

00:24:36.580 --> 00:24:38.180
Mary usually does the carving,

00:24:38.320 --> 00:24:42.590
but maybe tonight you'll do it, Henry.

00:24:44.810 --> 00:24:45.450
All right with you?

00:24:47.580 --> 00:24:57.710
Of course. I'd be happy to.

00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:10.440
Do I just cut them up like regular chickens?

00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:12.420
Sure, just cut them up like regular chickens.

00:25:37.360 --> 00:25:51.960
*Painful music*

00:26:00.960 --> 00:26:09.210
It'll be all right in a minute.

00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:51.350
Henry, what do you know?

00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:01.540
I don't know much of anything.

00:27:38.730 --> 00:27:41.490
Henry, may I speak to you a minute?

00:27:41.490 --> 00:27:43.860
Over here.

00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:37.750
Did you and Mary have sexual intercourse?

00:28:37.750 --> 00:28:41.770
Did you?

00:28:41.770 --> 00:28:43.330
Are you asking me this question?

00:28:43.330 --> 00:28:45.740
I have a very good reason.

00:28:45.740 --> 00:28:51.260
And now I want you to tell me.

00:28:51.260 --> 00:28:54.620
I'm very...

00:28:54.620 --> 00:28:55.620
I love Mary.

00:28:55.620 --> 00:28:59.570
Henry, I asked you if you and Mary had sexual intercourse.

00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:03.160
Well, I don't think that's any of your business.

00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:03.540
Harry!

00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:07.540
Sorry.

00:29:08.960 --> 00:29:13.810
Very bad trouble if you won't cooperate.

00:29:21.960 --> 00:29:26.360
Well, I...

00:29:26.360 --> 00:29:27.000
Mary!

00:29:32.170 --> 00:29:33.860
Answer me!

00:29:33.860 --> 00:29:35.400
I'm too nervous.

00:29:35.400 --> 00:29:36.730
There's a baby.

00:29:36.730 --> 00:29:38.380
It's at the hospital.

00:29:38.380 --> 00:29:40.360
Mom!

00:29:40.360 --> 00:29:41.360
And you're the father.

00:29:41.360 --> 00:29:43.050
That's impossible.

00:29:43.050 --> 00:29:44.050
It's only been--

00:29:44.050 --> 00:29:47.050
No, they're still not sure it is a baby.

00:29:47.050 --> 00:29:49.610
It's premature, but there's a baby.

00:29:49.610 --> 00:29:52.610
After the two of you are married, which should be very soon, you can pick the baby up.

00:30:16.890 --> 00:30:17.510
eyes.

00:30:30.540 --> 00:30:31.140
No.

00:30:36.470 --> 00:30:45.620
This dinner's getting mighty cold.

00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:45.330
No.

00:41:21.850 --> 00:41:28.630
are you talking about? I can't even sleep. I'm losing my mind. You're on vacation now.

00:41:28.630 --> 00:41:30.000
You can take care of it for a night.

00:41:32.560 --> 00:41:33.660
Well, you'll come back tomorrow?

00:41:35.520 --> 00:41:38.120
All I need is a decent best sleep.

00:41:41.560 --> 00:41:50.100
You need to just stay home.

00:41:51.670 --> 00:41:54.760
I'll do what I want to do.

00:42:30.600 --> 00:42:31.120
Okay.

00:52:34.220 --> 00:52:34.710
Come on.

00:53:30.540 --> 00:53:31.510
Move over.

00:54:08.190 --> 00:54:12.130
Over. Over.

00:58:22.810 --> 00:58:24.290
myself out of my apartment.

00:59:44.810 --> 00:59:49.500
Who is your wife?

00:59:49.500 --> 01:00:00.000
She must have gone back to her parents.

01:00:06.270 --> 01:00:07.040
Sure.

01:01:03.260 --> 01:01:04.680
I spend the night here.

